Lab 3.1 — Build & Audit a Secure File Server
Goal: Set up a small web-served directory tree with correct permissions

Create three users: alice, bob, svc_www
Create /srv/web/ with subfolders public, confidential, uploads
Set permissions so:
* public is readable by anyone
* confidential is only readable by alice and bob
* uploads is writable by svc_www but not world-writable
Give svc_www permission to restart a service via sudo, but only that command and nothing else
Run sudo -l -U svc_www and ls -la /srv/web/ to confirm

A setup.sh script that creates everything automatically, Include the output of find /srv/web -perm /o+w (should be empty).
